    "modification": "Removed three automatic fsck_hfs commands from restored_external, retaining partition readiness checks, USB initialization, kernel boot arguments and original read-only data mounting. Added a strict decimal --sleep SECONDS mode (0..3600) which returns before hardware initialization and resumes interrupted libc sleep calls. Verify the HFS root's device number against the /dev/md0 block device, accepting XNU's initial root_device label. Skip an already writable root; otherwise use a checked mount(2) update with the pinned XNU HFS arguments to avoid mount_hfs reopening the mounted RAM device. Disable stdout buffering at the start of the recovery program so progress reaches the display wrapper immediately; no recovery algorithm changes.",
